DCS 1
cast PARCELS
# The Parcels (REALM-CASTS.md): fenced fields, a delivery board for quests, deeds on the chain.

who Postmaster Grue
voice 2 0.9
step start
if route_done -> thanks
if route -> waiting
say Courier! The board's full and the Milk Cart Twins are two plots behind.
say There's a letter for Beekeeper Hollis, out past the sunflowers. Stamp it when it's in her hands.
ask Take the route? | I'll take it=accept | Not today=later
step accept
set route
give LETTER_GRUE 1
say Good. The stamp hammer's on your belt. Don't let the parcel shield get sticky.
end
step later
say The board doesn't empty itself. Come back when your boots are on.
end
step waiting
ask Delivered to Hollis yet? | Not yet=hint | Stamped and done=done
step hint
say Follow the fence posts north. Her hives hum; you'll hear them before you see them.
end
step done
set route_done
say That's a route done. Your name's on the board now. Next one pays in honey.
end
step thanks
say Best courier on the board. Grue says so, and Grue runs the board.
end

who Plot Surveyor Ilka
voice 6 1.0
step start
say Every parcel here is on the chain, number and all. Ten thousand of them, spiralling out from the hub.
ask Looking to claim one? | Show me the cheap ones=cheap | Show me the big ones=big | Just looking=no
step cheap
say Out on the far rings they're a song. Long walk to the board, though.
end
step big
say Estates: two by two, three by three, four by four. They never cross a district line. Rosa flies you over them.
end
step no
say Looking's free. The deeds aren't, and they don't come back once they're minted.
end

who Fence Smith
voice 1 0.85
step start
say Posts, latches, locks. A plot without a fence is a plot with everyone's goats in it.
ask What do you need? | Fence posts=posts | A gate latch=latch | Nothing today=no
step posts
say Twelve posts a side. Set them on your deed line; they won't set anywhere else.
end
step latch
say One latch per gate, and it only opens for the name on the deed. Or the goats, if you leave it swinging.
end
step no
say Mind the goats.
end

who Seed Broker Ott
voice 9 1.1
step start
say Stock changes with the weather. Rain lilies when it rains. Sunflowers when it doesn't.
ask Buying? | Wheat=wheat | Sunflower=sun | What's rare today?=rare
step wheat
say Wheat's always in. A week of sun and the Scarecrow hums to it.
end
step sun
say Hollis pays honey for a field of these. Plant them where the bees can find them.
end
step rare
say Rain lily, if it's raining. Is it raining? Look up. That's my whole trick.
end

who Scarecrow Elder
voice 0 0.7
step start
say ...The fields had songs once. Slow ones. The wheat liked them.
ask Would you sing one? | Please=sing | Another time=no
step sing
set field_song
say (The scarecrow sings, slow and low. Somewhere a field of wheat leans toward the sound.)
end
step no
say The fields will wait. They are good at it.
end

who Helipad Chief Rosa
voice 7 1.05
step start
if skid -> fitted
say The chopper's fuelled. Skids need work; you'll bounce off a fence post the way they are.
ask Fit the new skids? | Do it=fit | Fly as is=no
step fit
set skid
give HELI_SKID 1
say Done. Land on a post if you like. Don't land on the Crow.
end
step no
say Your bounce. Not mine.
end
step fitted
say Skids are holding. She's a good bird.
end

who Milk Cart Twins
voice 10 1.15
step start
say We're late. We're always late. Walk with us to the next plot and nothing will steal the milk.
ask Escort them? | Lead on=yes | Can't right now=no
step yes
set escort
say Stay close. The crows are bold here.
end
step no
say We'll go slow. We always go slow.
end

who Lost-Letter Ghost
voice 11 0.8
step start
say I carried a letter for a painter in the city of frames. I never got there. Would you?
ask Take the lost letter? | I'll deliver it=take | I can't cross realms=no
step take
set lost_letter
give LOST_LETTER 1
say Thank you. It's for someone called Vell. Tell them the Parcels remember.
end
step no
say Then it waits with me. We're both good at that now.
end

who Beekeeper Hollis
voice 5 1.0
step start
if route -> letter
say The hives are humming. A field of sunflowers would make them sing.
end
step letter
if route_done -> thanks
set route_done
give HONEY_JAR 2
say A letter? From Grue! Stamp it, courier; that's a route done. Here, honey for the road.
end
step thanks
say The honey's holding. Come back when the sunflowers are up.
end

who Auction Crow
voice 3 0.9
step start
say CAW. Everything sells. Seeds, deeds, honey, silence. What's yours?
ask Sell? | Seeds=seeds | Nothing, just the market talk=talk
step seeds
say Seeds are down. CAW. Everything is down until it's up.
end
step talk
say The Feud pair are both trying to sell the same fence. CAW. I'll take it twice.
end

who Weather Vane Keeper
voice 4 0.95
step start
say Storm by dusk. Wheat up a fifth, lilies in the broker's stall tomorrow. Write it down.
ask Will it hold? | Trust it=yes | Vanes lie=no
step yes
say Vanes don't lie. Keepers do, sometimes. Not today.
end
step no
say Then get wet. The vane won't mind.
end

who Neighbour Feud Pair
voice 8 1.1
step start
if side -> again
say THAT post is on MY line. - It is NOT. - Courier, you have the deed table. Whose is it?
ask Pick a side? | The left farmer=left | The right farmer=right | The deed decides=deed
step left
set side
say HA. - ...fine. The goats can have it.
end
step right
set side
say ...fine. - HA. The goats can have it.
end
step deed
set side
say The deed. - The deed. - (They both look at the table. Neither likes it. The goats have it.)
end
step again
say The goats have it. Everyone agrees. Nobody is happy.
end
